// XFAIL: RT-446b: UNSOUND: (RT-446's mechanism, a generic alias) a field `a: Rl<'static>` with `type Rl<'a> = &'a u64` takes a local's borrow: `Vg { a: &e }` returned from the fn is accepted; rustc E0597 (0.30.2)
// From the g302static work (its pre/pre04): a lifetime written through a
// type alias is not seen by the region walk (places::regions::bind_walk
// reads the type's AST node, and an alias's name has none), so a local's
// borrow fits a 'static place typed through an alias. Since v0.30.1 at
// least (it builds and prints 7, reading a dead stack slot). Forms:
// rt_446 a field `a: R` with `type R = &'static u64`, b `Rl<'static>`
// with `type Rl<'a> = &'a u64`, c `type S = W<'static>`, d a tuple
// alias, e an assignment `v.a = &e`, f `Vl<'static>` with a field
// `Rl<'a>`, g a fn's result `-> R` (pre03).
// FLAGS: --check-alloc
// ERROR: line 21
type Rl<'a> = &'a u64;

struct Vg {
    a: Rl<'static>,
}

fn generic_alias() -> Vg {
    let e = 7u64;
    Vg { a: &e }
}

fn main() {
    println("{}", generic_alias().a);
}
